 Shirley, Esq., M. P., for the numerous admirable Illustrations of the Dineley Tour; to the Rev. Samuel Hayman, A. M., for the woodcuts of the Earl of Cork’s monument, and of a Tradesman’s Token, struck at Youghal; d02131 1V PREFACE. to Captain Edward Hore, for an engraving of another Youghal Tradesman’s Token ; to Hodder Westropp, Esq., for a diagram illustrative of his paper on the resemblance between our Irish Round Towers and the French Fanaux de Cemetiére; to Major Dunne, and C. H. Doyne, Esq., for aid towards the plate of the Ancient Map of Irish Districts; to the Right Hon. John Wynne, for aid towards the plate of the Dromiskin find, and to the several contri- butors towards the Illustration Fund. The example of these be- nefactors to the Society is worthy of imitation. JAMES GRAVES. Rectory, Inisnae, March 22, 1864. CONTENTS. PART I.—1862. Proceedings, January Meeting, . .. . es a ; ; Extracts from the Journal of Thomas Dineley, Paibets giving an on of his Visit to Ireland in the Reign of Charles I. Continued. Communicated by Evelyn Philip Shirley, Esq., M. A., M. P., ‘ An Account of the Barony of Forth, in the County of Wexford, written at the close of the Seventeenth Century. Edited by Herbert F. Hore, Esq., . . ©. . ‘ ae eer Particulars relative t» Wexford and the Barony of Forth : by Colonel Solomon Richards, 1682. Edited by Herbert F. Hore, Esq, . . . «. ». 2 - © Proceedings, April Meeting, . . . by ask ts Rey “ae Fas See, . ae Extracts from the Journal of Thomas Dineley, Esquire, giving some eer of his Visit to Ireland in the Reign of Charles II. Continued. Communicated by Evelyn Philip Shirley, Esq., M. A., M. P. With Notes by the Rev. James Graves, A.B., M. R. 4 7. The Rental Book of Gerald Fitzgerald, Ninth Earl of Kildare. Begun in the year 1518. Continued. Edited by Herbert Francis Hore, Esq., . . BP tet ae ee Register of Historical Portraits. Continued. Edited by the Rev. James Graves, A. B.,M. R.A. . der Peete Proceedings, July Meeting, . . . . 