ac Mur- rough. A document in Harl. MS. 2138, as to the title to Fort O’ Nolan, quotes an inquest of 35, Edw. L, on Roger Bigod, Earl of Norfolk’s demesne estate there: this record mentions * one cham- ber of stone, one grange (now Grange- fort), 368 acres of demesne land (each acre is noted by the transcriber to cone tain five statute acres), worth yearly £12 5s. 4d., twenty acres of meadow; ten of pasture, called Oxynles, (i. e. the Oxen leys or meadows), and some other parcels of land. The Earl being an ab- sentee, and atter the O'Nolans had slain Edmond Mortimer, Earl of March and Ulster, in a skirmish at Kellistown, they recovered their country. 121 FrFoLio xiii. Obirnys Countrey.' riartagh M‘Philipp at Mid for eVy cow iiijd. at Michm’‘s. | In Killyneor for thef defen3 yevin by Mo- In Ardwoene yevin by ffergynanem M‘dongh for defen yerly of eVy cow iiiid. Vpon evy croe of shepe, i. Shepe. Vpon every croe of swyne, i. Swyn. In ye Brittas? at Mich yerly for ye defense yevin by Hugh Bradagh? t his kynesmencalled Gowil Shandowlyn‘, and also in evVy Towne The Moyntagh y‘of, Congho' Ogeran, Red. whiche shalbe inhited of their landf of eVy cow at Mich yerly iiiid. of eVy croe of shepe i, shepe ta dish of butt. And worke to the Castell of Cloghenogan. In the Leawn for the defenS at Mich yerly gevin by Hugh M‘Moriartagh xiiis. iiiid. In Ballyneglogh for_ye defenS yevin by Margty Enybryn® of eVy cow yerly at Mic niid. gevin by William Bedy and his kynesmen xlviii. galt butt?. In the Moyntagh of eVy acf at Michi iiijd. and of eVy cow iiijd. Upon Marglet Oge Enytholl® yerly for her defens at Hallontide viij galt hony. Upon Clan M‘Shane for ye detens yerly to ye said Erle t his heirs for eV graunted of evy cow iid. Itin upon Kylkeandragh and Kyllehighe or Patryke Archbolde, B. Kyllewyn iiijd upon eVy cow, yevin by the pson’ M’pluke yerly a shepe upon eVvy crow, t a swyne upon eVy crowe at Cristimas. Itm upon Clanm® Shan for thare defence yerly vnto the said Erle and his heir