. Itm vpon Clean Tean, . . . xxilij. kyne. 1“ Moynter-Tagane.”—Properly Mu- inter-Tadhgain, a district which was formed into the barony of Kilcourcy, and lies in the King’s County. 3“ Clancolman.”—That is to say, the country of the clan descended from Col- man. 3“ Calry.”"—The anglicised form of Calraighe. This name is retained and applied to a territory co-extensive with the parish of Ballyloughloe, in the ba- rony of Clonlonan, county of West- meath, Magawlcy was chieltain. Some interesting particulars respecting this territory are given ina note to the Irish ‘* Topographical Poems.” 4 Breawoyn.”— Properly Breagh- mhaine, now the barony of Brawney, in the west of the county of Westmeath. It belonged to the O’Breens. 5 i.e. for fines. 6“ Anayll."—Properly Anghaile, an- glicé the Annaly, a considerable terri- tury in the county of Longford, possess- ed by the Muintir-Fearghail, i.e., the family of O’Ferrall. David Spallan, reg. Inherit*unce. David Spallan, rec. Hugh M'Tege. Art M‘Edmond. Rathmore. Moygrilte. The Litil Raith. f 131 Ith vpon M°Morgh, . . . . xij. kyne. Itm vpon M*Heu oge, . . . xij. kyne. The abbot of Srougher yerly [is aan a Itt vpon Lisserdowle yerly, . xxvis. viijd. Itm the New Castell,,. . . . xxs. Itm Kylnecarra, . . . . . vis. viijd. Castel Broke to my Lord t% his Héyres;. a. <. 5 ee di we Vpon Feaghtne M*Cormok of Sleought Cowman in Keylte, vis. viijd. Itm Leysagh M°Hobert in Rath- asbik,. . . « . . «6 « Vis viijd. Itm the prio"of Monaster Deirge, vis. viijd. Itm vpé the castel and lande of the Barry- coribane ‘t Coricaysshill in pria de Analy in Conat ad festa Mit % festa Pasé annuatim equis porConib? ippm put pt [patet]iinden- — tura vna cii reVc6e déaf trar p*t decessi Kedagh O fferall ~ hered masé de corp’e suo legite pcf. Vpon the ca’ton of Oryncaghmore Clank- houghore, vis. viijd. Itm the cartron of Lesglassoke in Moybean from Hubte M*Caile ‘t Congho' Riogh is bro- ther to Geralde Erle of Kildare. Vpon Heu M*Tege M*Morirtagh in Clane- hou